latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Initialize:\n   - Create a deep copy of the input grid to modify.\n   - Get the dimensions of the grid (rows and columns).\n\n2. Identify unique colors:\n   - Iterate through the grid and create a set of all unique non-zero colors.\n\n3. For each unique color:\n   a. Find all occurrences:\n      - Create a list of (row, column) tuples for all occurrences of the color.\n   \n   b. Identify the topmost occurrence:\n      - Sort the occurrences list by row, then by column.\n      - The first element is the topmost occurrence.\n\n   c. Draw the main vertical line:\n      - Starting from the topmost occurrence, fill all cells in that column down to the bottom row with the color, unless the cell already has a non-zero color.\n\n   d. Connect other occurrences:\n      - For each occurrence (excluding the topmost):\n        - If it's not in the same column as the main vertical line:\n          - Draw a horizontal line in its row from its column to the main vertical line's column.\n\n   e. Connect in the bottom row:\n      - Find the leftmost and rightmost occurrences in the bottom row.\n      - If they exist and are different:\n        - Draw a horizontal line connecting them in the bottom row.\n\n4. Return the modified grid.\n\nAdditional considerations:\n\n5. Optimization (optional):\n   - Before step 3d, sort the occurrences by their distance to the main vertical line.\n   - This might help in reducing the total number of line segments in some cases.\n\n6. Error handling:\n   - Ensure the input grid is valid (rectangular, contains only integers 0-9).\n   - Handle edge cases like empty grids or grids with only one color.\n\n7. Testing:\n   - Apply this algorithm to all provided test cases.\n   - Create additional test cases to cover edge cases and more complex scenarios.\n\nThis plan should work for all cases presented and adheres to the rules of the challenge. It prioritizes vertical lines, connects all occurrences of each color, handles the bottom row specially, and should minimize the number of line segments used while ensuring all squares of the same color are connected."
